The T08 change is the Rust edit Brighton approved on 15 Nov. The router fallback and start-up check now use one constant, `SPA_FALLBACK_FILE = "200.html"`. The web adapter fallback moved to `200.html` in `web/vite.config.js`. The `rust-lessons.md` entry is appended.

## Blockers and notes
- **Deploy:** a server build and a `web/build` must be deployed together. An old build without `200.html` now fails the start-up check.
- **T13 and T14:** deferred E2E, recorded in `docs/kiro-log/landing-steel-night-blockers.md`.
- **Earlier decisions:** T02 font wiring reused `ide-workspace` fonts instead of new copies. The `<link rel="preload">` for Geist was not added. Lighthouse should decide if that matters.

## Review queue
No `[SUPERVISED]` tasks in this pass, so nothing was added to `landing-steel-night-review-queue.md`.

